%U A401993 560155062441443096413768480700,54540477209297439703018706108707771,11584969709437891822070264263918192374920
%N A401993 Number of strongly connected digraphs on n labeled nodes that are reducible as a flow graph rooted at node 1 and also rooted at node 2.
%C A401993 By label symmetry the count is the same for any fixed pair of roots: a(n) = R_2(n) = (1/binomial(n,2)) * Sum_j binomial(j,2) N_j(n), the second binomial moment of the valid-header distribution defined in A401321. R_1(n) = A397470(n) and R_n(n) = A400123(n); R_2 is the first genuinely two-rooted moment.
%C A401993 The roots are the fixed nodes 1 and 2; other nodes may also be valid headers. This does not count graphs with exactly two valid headers or graphs with a freely elected pair of roots. All digraphs here have no self-loops.
%D A401993 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Flow graph reducibility, SIAM J. Comput. 1 (1972), 188-202.
%D A401993 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Characterizations of reducible flow graphs, J. ACM 21 (1974), 367-375.
%D A401993 R. W. Robinson, Counting digraphs with restrictions on the strong components, in T.-H. Ku (ed.), Combinatorics and Graph Theory '95, World Scientific, Singapore, 1995, pp. 343-354.
%D A401993 R. E. Tarjan, Testing flow graph reducibility, J. Comput. System Sci. 9 (1974), 355-365.
%H A401993 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A401993/b401993.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 2..23</a>
%H A401993 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A398465/a398465.py.txt">Required Python module (labeled_reducible_cfgs.py)</a>, Jul 2026.
%H A401993 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A400123/a400123_1.py.txt">Required Python module (everywhere_reducible.py)</a>, Sep 2026.
%H A401993 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A401321/a401321_1.py.txt">Python program (valid_header_elections.py)</a>, Oct 2026.
%F A401993 a(n) = R_2(n) = (1/binomial(n,2)) * Sum_{j=2..n} binomial(j,2)*N_j(n), where N_j(n) is the number of strongly connected digraphs on n labeled nodes with exactly j valid headers.
%o A401993 (Python)
%o A401993 # Save the three linked Python files in one directory using the filenames
%o A401993 # shown in their link captions, then run Python in that directory.
%o A401993 from valid_header_elections import valid_header_sequence
%o A401993 valid_header_sequence("labeled_strong_two_valid_headers", 16)
